1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,608
Fifteen Points and Five Conditions

2
00:00:05,158 --> 00:00:08,726
On March 25, Pakistan delivered a fifteen-point U.S.

3
00:00:08,766 --> 00:00:12,680
ceasefire plan to Iran. According to Pakistani officials,

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:19,896
it offered sanctions relief in exchange for rolling back Iran's nuclear program, limits on its missiles,

5
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:22,810
and the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz.

6
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:30,052
The White House declined to discuss the plan, or to say whom in Iran it was negotiating with.

7
00:00:30,402 --> 00:00:37,684
That afternoon, Iranian state media, citing an unnamed senior official, said Iran rejected the American proposal.

8
00:00:37,724 --> 00:00:43,646
It laid out five conditions of its own: an end to attacks and to the killing of its leaders,

9
00:00:43,686 --> 00:00:49,802
guarantees that the war would not happen again, reparations, an end to fighting on every front,

10
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:53,832
and Iranian sovereignty over the Strait of Hormuz.

11
00:00:54,182 --> 00:01:01,847
Earlier that day, an Iranian drone hit the fuel depot at Kuwait International Airport, starting a large fire.

12
00:01:01,887 --> 00:01:04,816
Kuwait said it shot down six other drones.

13
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:09,481
The fire burned for three days and was not put out until March 28.

14
00:01:09,521 --> 00:01:18,188
Debris from an intercepted missile fell near Amman, and another missile landed in a field near Hadera in Israel.

15
00:01:18,538 --> 00:01:23,095
In Tehran, two cruise missile production sites were destroyed.

16
00:01:23,135 --> 00:01:27,099
In northwestern Iran, airstrikes killed eleven people.

17
00:01:27,139 --> 00:01:34,440
Iran claimed it fired cruise missiles at the carrier USS Abraham Lincoln; the ship was not damaged.

18
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:39,111
In western Anbar, a U.S. airstrike killed seven Iraqi soldiers.

19
00:01:39,151 --> 00:01:43,312
The papers were moving, and so were the bombs.

20
00:01:43,662 --> 00:01:46,543
One side said: give up what you have.

21
00:01:46,583 --> 00:01:49,939
The other said: pay for what you have done.

22
00:01:49,979 --> 00:01:53,808
Fifteen American points, five Iranian conditions.

23
00:01:53,848 --> 00:01:56,808
Only one word appeared on both papers.

24
00:01:56,848 --> 00:02:01,388
Hormuz. And the two countries meant opposite things by it.

25
00:02:01,428 --> 00:02:05,652
One paper went out, and one paper came back.

26
00:02:06,002 --> 00:02:09,843
Leila Shirazi had written her resignation three times.

27
00:02:09,883 --> 00:02:12,501
The first, the day South Pars burned.

28
00:02:12,541 --> 00:02:15,520
The second, the dawn after Natanz was hit.

29
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:18,897
The third, now, just before two in the morning.

30
00:02:18,937 --> 00:02:21,987
Each time she wrote it and did not save it.

31
00:02:22,027 --> 00:02:27,305
The cursor hovered over the button, she paused, and she closed the window.

32
00:02:27,345 --> 00:02:31,616
Tomorrow, then. Tomorrow was always another dawn.

33
00:02:31,966 --> 00:02:35,056
The fifteen points had crossed her desk too.

34
00:02:35,096 --> 00:02:42,027
The technical annex on the nuclear clauses: centrifuge counts, enrichment caps, inspection cycles.

35
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:44,161
She had written those numbers.

36
00:02:44,201 --> 00:02:51,701
Sentences from her own hand were now traveling through Islamabad to Tehran, the city where her aunt lived.

37
00:02:51,741 --> 00:02:54,689
The document went in the name of a nation.

38
00:02:54,729 --> 00:02:58,324
The numbers came from one person's hand.

39
00:02:58,674 --> 00:03:03,193
The list of sites for inspection: Natanz, Isfahan, Arak.

40
00:03:03,233 --> 00:03:07,508
And Fordow. The draft from above had left Fordow out.

41
00:03:07,548 --> 00:03:11,090
The reason was one line: already inoperable.

42
00:03:11,130 --> 00:03:13,533
She typed the word in herself.

43
00:03:13,573 --> 00:03:21,349
Then she wrote her cable. If a counterproposal comes with the rejection, the door is not closed.

44
00:03:21,389 --> 00:03:24,744
Do not kill the counterproposal.

45
00:03:25,094 --> 00:03:29,733
Five lines arrived. Leila read them in the original Persian.

46
00:03:29,773 --> 00:03:32,618
An end to attacks and assassinations.

47
00:03:32,658 --> 00:03:35,036
Guarantees against another war.

48
00:03:35,076 --> 00:03:38,311
Reparations. An end to war on every front.

49
00:03:38,351 --> 00:03:40,495
Sovereignty over the strait.

50
00:03:40,535 --> 00:03:48,449
Behind each sentence stood an old wound: the coup of 1953, eight years of war, the years of sanctions.

51
00:03:48,489 --> 00:03:53,372
Not an enemy's history. Her aunt's country's history.

52
00:03:53,722 --> 00:03:56,103
She opened the resignation file.

53
00:03:56,143 --> 00:03:58,146
This time she pressed save.

54
00:03:58,186 --> 00:04:00,265
Then she deleted it at once.

55
00:04:00,305 --> 00:04:03,821
Not tonight. The five lines had to be analyzed.

56
00:04:03,861 --> 00:04:08,210
She had to find a way to keep the Islamabad channel alive.

57
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:13,810
If she left, no one in this building would be left to read Fordow's pulse.

58
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:17,248
Midnight passed. She began to type.

59
00:04:17,598 --> 00:04:22,562
Ending assassinations and guarantees against recurrence: real demands.

60
00:04:22,602 --> 00:04:27,994
Reparations: leverage. Sovereignty over the strait: the wording cannot bend,

61
00:04:28,034 --> 00:04:32,211
but in practice it can be worked out through transit rules.

62
00:04:32,251 --> 00:04:34,356
And what was missing: nuclear.

63
00:04:34,396 --> 00:04:36,286
Not one word of enrichment.

64
00:04:36,326 --> 00:04:43,934
The documents that end wars usually come from the hands of those who wrote the documents that started them.

65
00:04:43,974 --> 00:04:44,724
— End of Episode 9. Continued in Episode 10. —

66
00:04:45,024 --> 00:04:49,668
Epic Fury continues in Episode 10.
